  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the dimensions of a rectangle whose area is $\\sqrt2\\,\\mathrm{m}^2$ and whose perimeter is $8\\,\\mathrm{m}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p18-q12-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\left(2-\\sqrt{4-\\sqrt2}\\right)\\mathrm{m}",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " by ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\left(2+\\sqrt{4-\\sqrt2}\\right)\\mathrm{m}",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p18-q12-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The side lengths sum to 4; solve ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "x^2-4x+\\sqrt2=0",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " using the quadratic formula.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let the side lengths be $x$ m and $y$ m, with $x,y>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2(x+y)&=8\\\\x+y&=4\\\\y&=4-x.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing the area,\n$$\\begin{align*}x(4-x)&=\\sqrt2\\\\4x-x^2&=\\sqrt2\\\\x^2-4x+\\sqrt2&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe quadratic formula gives\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac{4\\pm\\sqrt{16-4\\sqrt2}}{2}\\\\x&=2\\pm\\sqrt{4-\\sqrt2}.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $y=4-x$, the dimensions are $\\left(2-\\sqrt{4-\\sqrt2}\\right)$ m by $\\left(2+\\sqrt{4-\\sqrt2}\\right)$ m. Both are positive; their sum is $4$ and their product is $4-(4-\\sqrt2)=\\sqrt2$, as required.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
